  "title": "Air pollution link to GI cancers under scrutiny as Delhi sees patients as young as 15",
  "summary": "A 2026 review of 70 studies on air pollution and gastrointestinal diseases found that long-term exposure to fine particulate matter (PM2.5) was associated with higher mortality from GI cancers, with a notable association involving colorectal cancer.",
